AB  - Comprehensive impurity profiling of high-hazard pesticides like carbofuran remains challenging due to structural diversity, trace abundance, and technical limitations. This study developed an integrated analytical platform combining high performance liquid chromatography-diode array/charged aerosol detection (HPLC-DADCAD), Orbitrap high-resolution mass spectrometry (HRMS), and AI-driven computational tools (MSDIAL/SIRIUS) for systematic identification. HPLC-DAD-CAD resolved eight impurities, including seven chromophoric and one non-UV-absorbing species, while Orbitrap HRMS with data-dependent acquisition enabled sensitive fragmentation. Innovatively coupling MSDIAL (spectral deconvolution) and SIRIUS (sub-ppm molecular formula prediction/fragmentation modeling) identified three known impurities and five novel structures, tracing origins to synthesis byproducts and degradation pathways. MSDIAL eliminated spectral interference, enhancing structural annotation accuracy. Quantification at 280 nm minimized impurity interference, yielding carbofuran purity of 99.87 % with a combined uncertainty of 0.40 %, validated by quantitative NMR (99.78 %). This strategy bridges critical gaps in carbofuran reference material development and establishes a robust framework for impurity profiling of hazardous pesticides.
