AB  - The attendance, well-being and comfort of students is directly affected by the air quality in the classroom. Additionally, the performance of teachers and staff is also impacted by it. This drove us to embark on the project of developing a cloud-based system that can model and analyze the connection between indoor and outdoor air quality levels. The status of outdoor air is recognized to have a significant impact on indoor air quality. In this study, the link between indoor and outdoor air quality time series was exploited to construct a cloud-computing based system that calculates the indoor air quality index (IAQ) based on the locality's outside air quality index (AQI). Forecast models have been developed for assessing IAQ using outdoor AQI time series, by employing LightGBM, hybrid LightGBM-GRU and LightGBM-LSTM models. The performance of the forecast models is evaluated using mean percentage error (MPE), average absolute deviation (AAD), mean absolute percentage error (MAPE) and root mean square error (RMSE) metrics. The LightGBM-GRU based prediction model demonstrated the highest accuracy, achieving a MAPE of 1.76%.
