TI  - WOA-STMamba: A spatiotemporal Mamba model enhanced by Whale Optimization for short-term PM2.5 concentration prediction
T2  - JOURNAL OF ENVIRONMENTAL CHEMICAL ENGINEERING
LA  - English
KW  - PM2.5 Prediction
KW  - Deep Learning
KW  - Mamba
KW  - Swarm Intelligence Optimization
AB  - As industrialization and urbanization progress, PM2.5 pollution has become a pressing issue, demanding accurate forecasting. Existing models often struggle to capture complex spatiotemporal patterns and environmental dependencies. To address this, this study proposes WOA-STMamba, a spatiotemporal Mamba network enhanced by the Whale Optimization Algorithm (WOA). The model combines convolutional layers with a structured state-space Mamba backbone to extract rich spatiotemporal features. WOA dynamically optimizes the Mamba's selectivity mechanism-including core matrices A, B, C, and D-and globally tunes key hyperparameters such as convolution channels and learning rate. This enhances adaptability, generalization, and stability. In addition, a spatiotemporal correlation analysis is used to select relevant stations, improving long-range dependency modeling. The proposed model was validated using real-world data from 36 monitoring stations across Beijing. Compared to baseline methods including GRU, LSTM, STCN, and MICN, WOA-STMamba achieves lower RMSE and MAE, higher R2, and reduced training time. Specifically, it reduces RMSE by 4.67 %, MAE by 6.07 %, improves R2 by 0.57 %, and shortens the runtime per epoch to 18.96 s compared to MICN. The model also demonstrates strong robustness across seasons and stations. Ablation studies confirm the effectiveness of WOA and Mamba integration, while additional experiments on error distribution and uncertainty quantification further validate its stability and interpretability. The proposed method provides a reliable tool for PM2.5 forecasting and supports air pollution mitigation strategies. Code is available at this repository: https://github.com/Bubbles 929/WOA-STMamba.git.
