AB  - Accurate PM2.5 prediction is critical for effective air quality management. This study introduces a novel Bio-Inspired Hybrid LSTM model that synergizes Long Short-Term Memory networks with the Sparrow Search Algorithm (SSA) for intelligent hyperparameter optimization. Through comprehensive evaluation of five competing models using six pollutant indicators, our proposed SSA-LSTM demonstrates superior performance: achieving a remarkable 31.1% reduction in RMSE (8.601 vs 12.481 mu g/m3) and 7.0% improvement in R2 (0.946 vs 0.884) compared to baseline LSTM. The model consistently outperforms other hybrid approaches, showing a 2.9% RMSE advantage over PSO-LSTM (8.860 mu g/m3) and substantial 39.2% accuracy gains against CNN-LSTM architectures (14.138 mu g/m3). These results highlight SSA-LSTM's exceptional capability in escaping local optima while enhancing prediction robustness, establishing it as an advanced solution for environmental forecasting challenges. (c) 2025 Author(s). All article content, except where otherwise noted, is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivs 4.0 International (CC BY-NC-ND) license (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/).https://doi.org/10.1063/5.0287553
