AB  - With the expanding grid-connected photovoltaic capacity in western China, the threat of reduced output due to extensive dust storms increasingly jeopardizes grid reliability. Current photovoltaic forecasting methods neglect dust weather impacts, limiting accuracy. To address this, a novel prediction approach integrates satellite cloud imagery and PM10 concentration. A Convolutional Neural Network-Gated Recurrent Unit (CNN-GRU) model predicts PM10 levels, leveraging cloud data and historical meteorological records for precise forecasting. Additionally, a CNN-Attention-GRU model forecasts photovoltaic output during dust events, dynamically adjusting input weights based on PM10 concentration value (PM10) forecasts and Numerical Weather Prediction data via an attention mechanism. Tested in Northwest China, this method achieves 89.99% accuracy in short-term power predictions during dust scenarios, surpassing traditional methods by 1.53%.
